# Copy to `.env.capacitor`. Loaded only by `npm run build:capacitor`
# (Vite's `--mode capacitor`), layered on top of `.env`.
#
# The Android bundle has no server behind its https://localhost origin, so
# /api/* calls must be pointed at the deployed functions. This value is
# inlined into the JS at build time — it is a public URL, not a secret, but
# it does mean you must rebuild + `npx cap sync` to change it.
# tugtog.vercel.app and youtugtog.vercel.app are both aliases of the same
# Vercel project, so either works. Use the tugtog one: the old name contains a
# variant of "YouTube", which is what got com.youtugtog.app suspended, and the
# Play listing's Website and Privacy policy URLs are things a reviewer clicks.
# The old alias stays live so existing web users keep their saved queues, which
# are keyed to that origin in localStorage.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://tugtog.vercel.app
